From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Mon, 3 Aug 2026 10:42:55 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 08143/11362] [outer-loop] REPRODUCE defect B: the exp5766
 round-0 6.33x regression is a metric mismatch

The 6.33x gap reproduces exactly (exp5764 0.378487 / 12-of-13 nonzero games vs
exp5766 round-0 0.059829 / 2-of-13). It is not a mechanism regression.

Confounders VERIFIED rather than inherited: ROSTER, TRIALS, BUDGET, GGUF file,
KV quant and deployed n_ctx are all equal; both scripts call the same
atp.build_progress_window; induce succeeded 39/39 vs 38/39; the two induce
prompts are byte-identical apart from a 10-char pre-opened python fence.

What actually differs is two compounding things:

1. EVIDENCE. run_cegis_cell never passes proposal_transitions, so
   execute_bounded_llm_reinduction falls back to _proposal_prefix() -- the first
   2/3 of the window (REQ-ARC-WMTE-4557, deliberate). exp5764 passes the whole
   window. exp5766 round 0 is fit on a third less evidence.

2. GRADING. Same field name, two functions over two row sets. exp5764 scores
   WorldModelVerifier(whole window).accuracy, a set that OVERLAPS its prompt;
   exp5766 scores _score_accuracy(last 1/3), a set DISJOINT from its prompt.

Both quantities were recorded and only one of each was read: prefix_accuracy
sits beside heldout_accuracy in every exp5766 round record, and _proposal_prefix
and _split_prefix_heldout cut at the same index.

Scored like-for-like the arms are not distinguishable:
  reported          0.378487 vs 0.059829  ratio 6.3261  sign test p = 0.0386
  on shown rows     0.378487 vs 0.319444  ratio 1.1848  sign test p = 1.0
  reconstructed     0.378487 vs 0.293901  ratio 1.2878  sign test p = 1.0

Also found, load-bearing for anything downstream of this harness:

- 4 of 13 games (sp80, r11l, vc33, ft09) have a held-out tail with ZERO
  gradeable rows -- the only tail row is the level-up row, which score()
  excludes -- so accuracy = n_correct/max(1, n) returns 0.0 for EVERY engine.
  Verified with a perfect oracle; the control is non-vacuous (it scores 1.0 on
  real windows). Those zeros are unfalsifiable, not measurements.
- The tails carry 0-3 gradeable rows, so the primary within-loop delta_heldout
  can only move in steps of 1/3 at best, while its pre-registered gate is
  written in units of 0.15 and 0.05. The gate band is not expressible.
- Within exp5764 alone, games whose whole window fits under the prompt cap score
  0.6380 vs 0.1561 for those that exceed it (4.09x, exact permutation
  p = 0.0017) -- corroboration that its field behaves like a fit measure. The
  confound (window length is not randomly assigned) is stated in the artifact.

The residual 1.18-1.29x is NOT claimed to be zero. It is smaller than the
harness own documented ~40% cell-level nondeterminism (sampling_seed returns
None, so llama-server draws a fresh seed at temperature 0.2), and its sign is
what the one-third evidence handicap predicts.

Reproduction only -- no upstream code changed, no default flipped, nothing
submitted. results/arc_e3 and sibling fixture trees are checksum-verified
byte-identical across the run (148 files). adversarial_verify and
summarize_artifact both clean. The four tests are mutation-verified: flipping
the split, making an empty denominator report 1.0, and removing the prefix
handicap each turn the suite red.

